1
00:00:01,233 --> 00:00:03,033
Pretty good, right?

2
00:00:05,467 --> 00:00:06,167
I see.

3
00:00:06,267 --> 00:00:08,033
Rock thinks so too.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:09,500
It's delicious.

5
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:11,020
Today's miso soup is really good.

6
00:00:11,467 --> 00:00:11,967
Oh?

7
00:00:12,333 --> 00:00:13,333
You can tell?

8
00:00:13,467 --> 00:00:15,067
I changed the miso.

9
00:00:15,167 --> 00:00:16,533
I'm amazing.

10
00:00:17,067 --> 00:00:18,067
Hey.

11
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,867
What time does your tutoring start today?

12
00:00:20,433 --> 00:00:21,433
Hmm...

13
00:00:21,467 --> 00:00:21,933
3 o'clock.

14
00:00:22,033 --> 00:00:23,300
3 o'clock, huh?

15
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:24,600
I have to work then.

16
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:26,673
I won't get to see Sota again today.

17
00:00:26,767 --> 00:00:30,167
We're making sweets in cooking class today.
I'll bring some back for you guys later.

18
00:00:30,267 --> 00:00:31,267
What kind of sweets?

19
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:34,600
- Dango.
- You don't need tutoring anymore, right?

20
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:36,667
Huh?

21
00:00:36,933 --> 00:00:38,667
You did well on your mock exams.

22
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:40,667
That's enough, isn't it?

23
00:00:41,367 --> 00:00:42,367
What do you mean, enough?

24
00:00:42,433 --> 00:00:44,367
There are still five
months until the exams.

25
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,567
Just go to a cram school.

26
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,867
The whole point of getting a tutor was
to improve your mock exam scores.

27
00:00:52,133 --> 00:00:52,600
Huh?

28
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:53,767
Is that so?

29
00:00:53,867 --> 00:00:55,800
I don't remember agreeing to that.

30
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:56,733
Yeah.

31
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,833
That was my plan all along.

32
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:00,167
You said it yourself, honey.

33
00:01:00,267 --> 00:01:02,467
Didn't you say Sota-san is a great teacher?

34
00:01:02,567 --> 00:01:03,567
Rio.

35
00:01:03,633 --> 00:01:06,967
Tell the teacher he doesn't
need to come anymore.

36
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:07,467
What?

37
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:08,667
What? Starting today?

38
00:01:08,767 --> 00:01:09,333
Exactly.

39
00:01:09,433 --> 00:01:11,100
Hold on a second, honey.

40
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:12,767
That's way too unreasonable.

41
00:01:15,933 --> 00:01:17,100
Um.

42
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:18,200
About the tutoring fees.

43
00:01:18,733 --> 00:01:21,833
I'll get a part-time job and pay
you back once I get into college.

44
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:24,333
It's not about the money.

45
00:01:25,467 --> 00:01:27,867
Then you have no reason to object.

46
00:01:28,633 --> 00:01:30,100
I'm just studying.

47
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,867
It's not like I'm doing anything wrong.

48
00:01:31,967 --> 00:01:32,967
This.

49
00:01:33,533 --> 00:01:34,800
Is my house.

50
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,200
Fine, I get it.

51
00:01:39,133 --> 00:01:40,576
Then we just won't
have the lessons at home.

52
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,280
Do you really want to continue that badly?

53
00:01:45,567 --> 00:01:46,567
Lately...

54
00:01:47,067 --> 00:01:50,367
I've actually started to enjoy math.

55
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:54,667
It makes me want to learn more.

56
00:01:54,767 --> 00:01:56,033
It's really unlike me.

57
00:01:56,133 --> 00:01:57,633
Is math...

58
00:01:58,267 --> 00:01:59,587
The only thing you've fallen for?

59
00:02:00,633 --> 00:02:01,633
Huh?

60
00:02:01,767 --> 00:02:02,767
What do you mean?

61
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:04,967
Anyway.

62
00:02:07,433 --> 00:02:08,333
I won't allow it.

63
00:02:08,433 --> 00:02:10,133
Why are you so against this?

64
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,067
Did I do something wrong?

65
00:02:17,367 --> 00:02:18,800
What's up with Dad?

66
00:02:22,367 --> 00:02:24,367
Did something happen with Sota?

67
00:02:24,467 --> 00:02:25,933
I don't think so.

68
00:02:26,033 --> 00:02:27,309
When Sota-san stayed over last time,

69
00:02:27,333 --> 00:02:29,067
Your dad had a great time talking with him.

70
00:02:29,167 --> 00:02:30,700
He really liked him.

71
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,080
Then why is he acting like this?

72
00:02:33,533 --> 00:02:34,667
Don't tell me...

73
00:02:36,267 --> 00:02:38,833
Did he find out about Natsuki and him?

74
00:02:38,933 --> 00:02:39,967
No way.

75
00:02:40,067 --> 00:02:42,100
I hope not too.

76
00:02:44,467 --> 00:02:45,667
What is going on?

77
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,633
Stupid old man.

78
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:04,967
"Your Summer, My Storm"
(Episode 9)

79
00:03:12,967 --> 00:03:15,133
(Exchange Program)

80
00:03:25,567 --> 00:03:27,200
(Global Internship Joint Briefing)

81
00:03:28,467 --> 00:03:29,467
Huh?

82
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:37,567
What?

83
00:03:37,667 --> 00:03:38,667
What's wrong?

84
00:03:39,533 --> 00:03:40,733
Have a seat.

85
00:03:41,367 --> 00:03:42,367
Huh?

86
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:48,233
Natsuki.

87
00:03:48,333 --> 00:03:51,633
Did Dad ever look at your phone,

88
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:55,767
Or overhear you on a call or something?

89
00:03:55,867 --> 00:03:58,100
What do you mean?

90
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:00,167
About Sota.

91
00:04:00,267 --> 00:04:01,267
Huh?

92
00:04:01,833 --> 00:04:04,167
Dad might have found out.

93
00:04:04,267 --> 00:04:06,167
No... wait a second.

94
00:04:06,267 --> 00:04:07,067
Ah.

95
00:04:07,167 --> 00:04:09,400
Mom knows how you feel.

96
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:10,067
Huh?

97
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:11,200
I'm sorry.

98
00:04:11,667 --> 00:04:16,233
I accidentally overheard you guys
talking about Sota-san earlier.

99
00:04:16,333 --> 00:04:17,600
Ah... huh?

100
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:20,067
It's okay.

101
00:04:21,333 --> 00:04:24,600
Mom is on your side.

102
00:04:27,033 --> 00:04:28,833
Our generation,

103
00:04:28,933 --> 00:04:30,343
Isn't very familiar
with this sort of thing.

104
00:04:30,367 --> 00:04:33,100
Our way of thinking might be a bit behind.

105
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:36,700
She's even been asking
AI to learn more about it.

106
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,467
Even when I ask amateur questions,

107
00:04:39,567 --> 00:04:42,767
It doesn't judge me
and teaches me patiently.

108
00:04:42,867 --> 00:04:44,800
It's really been a big help.

109
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,400
Huh?

110
00:04:53,067 --> 00:04:54,067
Natsuki?

111
00:04:54,567 --> 00:04:56,667
Wait, why are you crying?

112
00:04:56,767 --> 00:04:57,767
It's just...

113
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:02,400
Because... Mom and you,

114
00:05:05,467 --> 00:05:06,967
Are both so good to me...

115
00:05:10,267 --> 00:05:12,267
Haven't we always been good to you?

116
00:05:13,867 --> 00:05:15,100
Hey.

117
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:17,867
Have you been feeling anxious?

118
00:05:22,867 --> 00:05:23,733
Yeah.

119
00:05:23,833 --> 00:05:25,500
It's okay.

120
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,267
It's completely normal.

121
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:31,533
Love always comes with a little anxiety.

122
00:05:37,333 --> 00:05:39,000
Mom...

123
00:05:42,767 --> 00:05:43,767
Honestly.

124
00:05:45,767 --> 00:05:46,867
Stop crying.

125
00:05:46,967 --> 00:05:47,967
There, there.

126
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:50,800
It's all right...

127
00:05:53,733 --> 00:05:55,100
That's amazing.

128
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:56,767
I know, right?

129
00:06:02,233 --> 00:06:04,467
(Men...)

130
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:10,767
(Romance between men)

131
00:06:12,067 --> 00:06:14,967
(Related images)

132
00:06:15,467 --> 00:06:16,667
Good work.

133
00:06:16,767 --> 00:06:18,100
Ah, good work.

134
00:06:19,967 --> 00:06:21,033
Is your meeting over?

135
00:06:21,133 --> 00:06:22,533
Senpai, you've got a smudge here.

136
00:06:22,633 --> 00:06:23,867
Sorry, thanks.

137
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:25,367
Be more careful.

138
00:06:35,533 --> 00:06:36,167
Hello?

139
00:06:36,267 --> 00:06:37,267
It's me.

140
00:06:37,633 --> 00:06:38,467
Oh.

141
00:06:38,567 --> 00:06:39,567
Na-chan.

142
00:06:40,667 --> 00:06:41,867
I see...

143
00:06:41,967 --> 00:06:44,533
So your parents both know.

144
00:06:44,633 --> 00:06:47,767
But I have no idea how my dad found out.

145
00:06:49,633 --> 00:06:50,633
Ah.

146
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:53,300
Could he have seen our
photo booth pictures?

147
00:06:55,133 --> 00:06:57,733
Hmm... it's not impossible.

148
00:06:57,833 --> 00:06:58,967
That's probably it, right?

149
00:06:59,067 --> 00:07:00,067
Huh?

150
00:07:00,533 --> 00:07:02,900
But even if he saw them,
would it really be a problem?

151
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:03,900
But,

152
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,633
For our parents' generation,

153
00:07:05,733 --> 00:07:08,733
Just seeing two guys taking pictures
like that might be off-putting to them.

154
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,133
I see.

155
00:07:11,033 --> 00:07:11,933
Besides...

156
00:07:12,033 --> 00:07:14,567
Looking at these is a bit embarrassing.

157
00:07:15,167 --> 00:07:16,800
It makes me want to smile.

158
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:20,000
Yeah... me too.

159
00:07:20,433 --> 00:07:24,567
Maybe he picked up on that vibe?

160
00:07:27,833 --> 00:07:29,067
That makes sense.

161
00:07:31,167 --> 00:07:35,100
My sister and mom accepted it right away.

162
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:41,800
But Dad just can't understand
anything that goes against his values.

163
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,533
I think everyone in my
family would be the same.

164
00:07:45,633 --> 00:07:46,633
So,

165
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:49,600
Rio and your mom are really amazing.

166
00:07:50,933 --> 00:07:51,933
You think so?

167
00:07:54,632 --> 00:07:57,866
But whatever, we can just ignore
that stupid old man.

168
00:07:57,967 --> 00:07:59,543
We don't have to do the
tutoring at home anyway.

169
00:07:59,567 --> 00:08:01,900
It's not good to do this
behind your dad's back.

170
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,367
Don't give me that model student talk.

171
00:08:04,467 --> 00:08:05,867
That's not what I meant.

172
00:08:07,733 --> 00:08:11,300
I really like your family, Na-chan.

173
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:13,767
I don't want to tear you guys apart.

174
00:08:24,067 --> 00:08:25,467
I'm sorry.

175
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:27,100
Huh?

176
00:08:27,567 --> 00:08:30,467
You didn't even do anything wrong, So-chan,

177
00:08:30,567 --> 00:08:31,833
Yet you have to deal with this.

178
00:08:31,933 --> 00:08:34,600
No, you didn't do anything
wrong either, Na-chan.

179
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,500
Let's figure this out together.

180
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:40,600
Okay?

181
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:44,900
Yeah.

182
00:08:45,567 --> 00:08:46,700
- This is so good.
- Right?

183
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:47,809
It's not too sweet. It's delicious.

184
00:08:47,833 --> 00:08:49,333
Ah, Yanagi-san.

185
00:08:49,433 --> 00:08:49,833
Yes?

186
00:08:49,933 --> 00:08:53,433
Could you take these
to Natsuki and Riku later?

187
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:54,533
No problem.

188
00:08:54,633 --> 00:08:57,867
We have to pick the prettiest
ones for Na-chan and the others.

189
00:08:57,967 --> 00:08:58,767
Definitely.

190
00:08:58,867 --> 00:09:02,433
We have to thank them for
nourishing the hearts of us fans.

191
00:09:02,533 --> 00:09:03,733
Is this one okay?

192
00:09:03,833 --> 00:09:05,167
Well...

193
00:09:05,267 --> 00:09:07,033
By the way, is this okay?

194
00:09:13,133 --> 00:09:14,233
What's wrong?

195
00:09:14,333 --> 00:09:15,867
You seem a bit down today.

196
00:09:16,767 --> 00:09:17,833
Let me tell you...

197
00:09:17,933 --> 00:09:20,933
I've decided to choose Umi-kun.

198
00:09:21,033 --> 00:09:24,367
Ah... you mean about
having three people you like?

199
00:09:24,467 --> 00:09:25,233
Yeah.

200
00:09:25,333 --> 00:09:26,967
So you decided on Umi-kun.

201
00:09:27,067 --> 00:09:27,567
Yeah.

202
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,767
Because I have the most fun
when I'm playing with Umi-kun.

203
00:09:33,267 --> 00:09:34,267
I see.

204
00:09:35,067 --> 00:09:37,200
But... then...

205
00:09:38,167 --> 00:09:39,167
Hmm?

206
00:09:40,767 --> 00:09:45,767
Someone said it's weird
for a boy to like a boy.

207
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Natsuki.

208
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,800
Am I weird?

209
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:02,767
You're not weird at all.

210
00:10:03,333 --> 00:10:04,333
Really?

211
00:10:04,367 --> 00:10:05,567
Yeah.

212
00:10:05,967 --> 00:10:08,033
The person who called
you weird is the weird one.

213
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:09,600
But...

214
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:12,633
Did Umi-kun say you were weird too?

215
00:10:13,733 --> 00:10:15,767
Umi-kun said he was happy.

216
00:10:16,633 --> 00:10:17,833
Then that's all that matters.

217
00:10:18,467 --> 00:10:19,467
I see.

218
00:10:23,333 --> 00:10:24,933
Everyone is different,

219
00:10:25,033 --> 00:10:27,500
and everyone is special.

220
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:28,900
That startled me.

221
00:10:30,733 --> 00:10:32,267
It takes all kinds to make a world.

222
00:10:32,367 --> 00:10:35,367
If everyone were exactly the same,
the world would be so boring.

223
00:10:35,467 --> 00:10:38,100
It's our differences that
make things interesting.

224
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:39,600
That makes sense.

225
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:41,000
Say it again.

226
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:42,800
Did you guys fight again?

227
00:10:43,133 --> 00:10:45,767
It wasn't really a fight.

228
00:10:46,033 --> 00:10:48,167
His mindset is just so outdated.

229
00:10:48,267 --> 00:10:49,767
It really ticks me off.

230
00:10:49,867 --> 00:10:50,500
That happens all the time.

231
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:52,300
My husband is the exact same way.

232
00:10:52,533 --> 00:10:55,933
You can't just blame
it on their age, either.

233
00:10:56,167 --> 00:10:58,209
Are there parents like that
at the kindergarten too?

234
00:10:58,233 --> 00:10:59,567
Oh, definitely.

235
00:10:59,933 --> 00:11:04,733
We have a few kids at the kindergarten
who are foreign or use wheelchairs.

236
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,933
Quite a few parents complain about it.

237
00:11:07,033 --> 00:11:11,633
They say it's not good to have them
in the same class as the regular kids.

238
00:11:11,967 --> 00:11:13,367
That sounds exhausting.

239
00:11:13,467 --> 00:11:15,367
How do you handle it when that happens?

240
00:11:15,467 --> 00:11:18,000
If it actually caused a problem,
that would be one thing.

241
00:11:18,367 --> 00:11:22,233
But we tell the parents we won't accept
one-sided discrimination.

242
00:11:22,633 --> 00:11:24,567
Still, it's hard to get them to understand.

243
00:11:24,667 --> 00:11:26,933
So things are still like that nowadays.

244
00:11:27,233 --> 00:11:28,700
Are those kids doing okay?

245
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:31,433
Kids are actually very
sensitive. They easily notice

246
00:11:31,533 --> 00:11:33,213
if people are looking at them differently.

247
00:11:33,267 --> 00:11:34,367
Yeah.

248
00:11:34,667 --> 00:11:35,909
That's why I always try to
keep a close eye on them.

249
00:11:35,933 --> 00:11:37,076
But this kind of prejudice...

250
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:40,367
It's probably a lot less
common than when I was a kid.

251
00:11:40,467 --> 00:11:43,000
Did you have some bad experiences
in the past, Kaoru-san?

252
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:45,200
It wasn't a big deal.

253
00:11:45,300 --> 00:11:47,300
It's just that my parents got divorced.

254
00:11:47,533 --> 00:11:50,043
When I was little, my dad was the one
who dropped me off and picked me up.

255
00:11:50,067 --> 00:11:51,433
Back then, just doing that

256
00:11:51,533 --> 00:11:53,567
was enough to get you weird looks.

257
00:11:53,667 --> 00:11:55,733
That is a big deal, Kaoru-san.

258
00:11:55,833 --> 00:11:57,100
That's really awful.

259
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,967
It's hard to imagine that now.

260
00:11:59,067 --> 00:12:01,167
But thanks to that,

261
00:12:01,267 --> 00:12:03,309
I learned from a young age that
other people are other people,

262
00:12:03,333 --> 00:12:05,833
and I am me.

263
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:07,373
So I guess some good came out of it.

264
00:12:08,067 --> 00:12:08,933
That's amazing.

265
00:12:09,033 --> 00:12:10,943
I hope the kids at our kindergarten
can understand that too.

266
00:12:10,967 --> 00:12:12,900
There are so many people in this world

267
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,133
with different backgrounds
and ways of thinking.

268
00:12:16,233 --> 00:12:17,067
If they can learn that,

269
00:12:17,167 --> 00:12:20,933
wouldn't this world
become a little easier to live in?

270
00:12:21,033 --> 00:12:22,033
Exactly.

271
00:12:23,233 --> 00:12:24,833
It really would.

272
00:12:27,567 --> 00:12:30,400
Should I go apologize to his father?

273
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:33,333
There's no need to apologize.

274
00:12:33,433 --> 00:12:35,233
You haven't done anything wrong.

275
00:12:35,333 --> 00:12:36,333
But...

276
00:12:36,367 --> 00:12:38,100
Please be more specific.

277
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:39,200
Ah...

278
00:12:39,833 --> 00:12:43,067
It's not like I completely
fail to understand his father's feelings.

279
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,533
You say you don't fail to understand.

280
00:12:45,633 --> 00:12:47,900
Does that mean you can empathize with him?

281
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:48,733
No.

282
00:12:48,833 --> 00:12:50,167
Empathizing...

283
00:12:50,267 --> 00:12:53,000
That doesn't feel quite right.

284
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,033
Please be more specific.

285
00:13:05,167 --> 00:13:06,633
Let's figure this out together.

286
00:13:16,867 --> 00:13:17,867
Okay.

287
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:19,633
Why isn't Dad back yet?

288
00:13:21,567 --> 00:13:23,233
After saying all those things,

289
00:13:23,333 --> 00:13:25,067
he's probably too embarrassed to come home.

290
00:13:25,667 --> 00:13:26,709
A little late to be embarrassed now...

291
00:13:26,733 --> 00:13:28,067
I'm taking Rock for a walk.

292
00:13:28,167 --> 00:13:29,167
Huh?

293
00:13:30,933 --> 00:13:31,933
Let's go, Rock.

294
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:33,833
I'm heading out.

295
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:36,067
Be careful.

296
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:38,467
I'm going to go get Dad.

297
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:47,600
You're a fast runner, Rock.

298
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:54,967
Rock.

299
00:13:55,067 --> 00:13:56,600
You have to protect me, okay?

300
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:00,900
Ah.

301
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:15,100
You're back.

302
00:14:17,467 --> 00:14:18,533
I'm back.

303
00:14:21,167 --> 00:14:22,167
Rock.

304
00:14:22,633 --> 00:14:23,533
Good boy.

305
00:14:23,633 --> 00:14:24,667
I'm back.

306
00:14:24,767 --> 00:14:26,233
Okay, good boy.

307
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:29,033
Rock.

308
00:14:29,133 --> 00:14:30,733
You're running too fast.

309
00:14:30,833 --> 00:14:31,833
Geez.

310
00:14:38,833 --> 00:14:39,833
Um...

311
00:14:44,100 --> 00:14:45,133
All this time...

312
00:14:46,733 --> 00:14:50,200
I've never truly liked anyone before.

313
00:14:55,433 --> 00:14:58,267
I'm only just now realizing that.

314
00:15:01,333 --> 00:15:02,333
Now...

315
00:15:08,867 --> 00:15:11,467
Because I've finally
truly fallen for someone.

316
00:15:15,667 --> 00:15:18,500
Um, you...

317
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:21,500
I don't like him because he's a man.

318
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:26,633
And the people I dated before,

319
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:30,500
it wasn't because they were women
that I couldn't fall for them.

320
00:15:32,733 --> 00:15:33,733
The person I like

321
00:15:34,267 --> 00:15:37,500
is Kobayakawa Sota.

322
00:15:42,967 --> 00:15:47,100
Talking to my parents about
this is embarrassing as hell.

323
00:15:49,033 --> 00:15:51,133
But if I don't spell it out,
you won't understand.

324
00:15:55,567 --> 00:15:57,533
Do you think it's disgusting?

325
00:15:59,767 --> 00:16:01,433
It does make me uncomfortable.

326
00:16:05,267 --> 00:16:07,067
It's fine if you don't understand.

327
00:16:09,233 --> 00:16:10,533
But...

328
00:16:13,267 --> 00:16:17,200
I hope you won't look
at So-chan with prejudice.

329
00:16:19,267 --> 00:16:20,633
So-chan...

330
00:16:22,567 --> 00:16:25,133
just happens to be the person I fell for.

331
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:33,100
Huh? Rock, what's wrong?

332
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:37,400
Huh?

333
00:16:37,667 --> 00:16:38,667
Huh?

334
00:16:39,167 --> 00:16:41,067
Ah, hello.

335
00:16:41,167 --> 00:16:42,467
Huh? What are you doing here?

336
00:16:42,567 --> 00:16:44,000
I went to your house,

337
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:48,333
and they said you took Rock to
the station to pick up your dad.

338
00:16:48,567 --> 00:16:50,167
Why did you go to my house?

339
00:16:51,133 --> 00:16:53,267
Because I wanted to talk to your dad.

340
00:17:02,667 --> 00:17:03,667
Um...

341
00:17:08,767 --> 00:17:10,867
If my presence makes you uncomfortable,

342
00:17:11,967 --> 00:17:13,900
I won't come to your house anymore.

343
00:17:14,767 --> 00:17:17,167
I'll do my best to stay out of your sight.

344
00:17:23,533 --> 00:17:24,800
So...

345
00:17:30,133 --> 00:17:32,700
I hope your family can stay the way it was.

346
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:39,033
The Takemiya family is so warm.

347
00:17:39,833 --> 00:17:41,600
Everyone is so kind.

348
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:45,900
It's the kind of family
I've always dreamed of.

349
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,667
So,

350
00:17:49,533 --> 00:17:52,467
I hope you can all
stay exactly as you are.

351
00:17:53,467 --> 00:17:55,000
Please.

352
00:18:00,967 --> 00:18:02,533
I'm really sorry

353
00:18:02,633 --> 00:18:05,200
for stopping you
and saying such presumptuous things.

354
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:14,400
What about you? Um...

355
00:18:15,267 --> 00:18:18,533
How do you feel about Natsuki?

356
00:18:18,633 --> 00:18:20,533
I don't know yet.

357
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:23,033
Huh?

358
00:18:23,133 --> 00:18:26,333
I definitely have feelings for Natsuki.

359
00:18:26,967 --> 00:18:30,833
But... whether it's friendship or love,

360
00:18:31,133 --> 00:18:32,133
or admiration,

361
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:34,100
I can't even tell myself.

362
00:18:35,267 --> 00:18:36,267
I'm sorry.

363
00:18:39,167 --> 00:18:40,300
Then you...

364
00:18:42,033 --> 00:18:44,267
Um... uh...

365
00:18:44,767 --> 00:18:46,167
I've never...

366
00:18:46,267 --> 00:18:49,067
fallen for a guy before.

367
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:51,200
Is that so?

368
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:52,500
Yes.

369
00:18:53,967 --> 00:18:55,067
It's just that...

370
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:58,933
when I'm with Natsuki,

371
00:19:00,033 --> 00:19:01,300
I'm truly happy.

372
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:03,033
I'm even surprised myself

373
00:19:04,067 --> 00:19:07,967
that I can smile like this.

374
00:19:10,967 --> 00:19:13,133
Meeting someone like him...

375
00:19:14,933 --> 00:19:17,467
I feel incredibly lucky.

376
00:19:36,067 --> 00:19:37,067
Rock.

377
00:19:37,133 --> 00:19:38,133
Let's go home.

378
00:19:38,833 --> 00:19:40,067
Come on.

379
00:19:40,733 --> 00:19:41,800
Okay.

380
00:19:41,900 --> 00:19:42,900
Let's go.

381
00:19:52,233 --> 00:19:53,867
What are you standing around for?

382
00:19:55,267 --> 00:19:56,267
Go on.

383
00:19:58,667 --> 00:19:59,867
But...

384
00:20:00,433 --> 00:20:01,867
You come too, Teacher.

385
00:20:03,667 --> 00:20:05,033
Huh?

386
00:20:05,633 --> 00:20:09,033
If you haven't had dinner yet...

387
00:20:09,967 --> 00:20:10,500
Huh?

388
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:12,167
You know how our house is.

389
00:20:12,267 --> 00:20:13,633
You know how my wife is.

390
00:20:13,733 --> 00:20:16,600
She's definitely already
prepared something.

391
00:20:18,833 --> 00:20:20,000
Let's go, Rock.

392
00:20:22,733 --> 00:20:23,733
So-chan.

393
00:20:26,667 --> 00:20:27,667
Okay.

394
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:30,167
Let's go, Rock.

395
00:20:31,433 --> 00:20:33,400
The stew is really good today.

396
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:34,000
Did you get some meat?

397
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,767
Yeah, it's so good.

398
00:20:35,867 --> 00:20:37,747
I've just been eating the
meat and potato stew.

399
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:39,667
It really is delicious.

400
00:20:39,767 --> 00:20:42,200
I'm stuffed.

401
00:20:42,733 --> 00:20:43,500
That was so good.

402
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:44,833
It really was delicious.

403
00:20:44,933 --> 00:20:46,233
I'm so happy.

404
00:20:46,333 --> 00:20:47,733
It's actually really easy to make.

405
00:20:47,833 --> 00:20:49,467
I'll give you the recipe later.

406
00:20:49,567 --> 00:20:50,133
Really?
Of course.

407
00:20:51,067 --> 00:20:52,100
Thank you, Mrs. Takemiya.

408
00:20:52,867 --> 00:20:54,033
That's great.

409
00:20:54,933 --> 00:20:55,800
Let me help.

410
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:56,967
Oh, thank you.

411
00:20:57,067 --> 00:20:58,067
I'll wash them.

412
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:00,809
- Oh, then I'll handle these.
- Alright, you two don't need to fuss.

413
00:21:00,833 --> 00:21:02,943
- I'll do it later, just leave it for now.
- It's fine.

414
00:21:02,967 --> 00:21:03,867
Please let me help.
Give it to me.

415
00:21:04,667 --> 00:21:05,433
Here.

416
00:21:05,533 --> 00:21:07,167
- Um...
- Is this the dish soap?

417
00:21:08,167 --> 00:21:11,500
You startled me, honey. You've
suddenly made so much progress.

418
00:21:11,867 --> 00:21:13,267
I didn't even do anything.

419
00:21:13,533 --> 00:21:16,100
You were such a super stubborn dad
just this morning.

420
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:20,300
Why the sudden change of heart?

421
00:21:22,233 --> 00:21:23,953
I wouldn't say I've completely accepted it.

422
00:21:25,433 --> 00:21:26,867
Really?

423
00:21:26,967 --> 00:21:28,267
To be honest,

424
00:21:28,900 --> 00:21:30,567
I still don't really get it.

425
00:21:30,667 --> 00:21:34,400
But they both spoke from the heart.

426
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:37,767
I could feel their sincerity.

427
00:21:37,867 --> 00:21:39,367
So you want to support them now?

428
00:21:39,467 --> 00:21:41,800
I'm not planning on giving
them a push or anything.

429
00:21:41,900 --> 00:21:44,900
Meaning you're starting
to try and understand?

430
00:21:45,267 --> 00:21:46,267
Yeah.

431
00:21:46,733 --> 00:21:47,800
Something like that.

432
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:50,200
That's good enough.

433
00:21:51,433 --> 00:21:55,233
As long as you can understand
a little bit someday, that's fine.

434
00:21:56,633 --> 00:21:57,633
Yeah.

435
00:21:59,300 --> 00:22:01,167
Hey, you're splashing me.

436
00:22:01,267 --> 00:22:02,467
No, I'm not.

437
00:22:02,567 --> 00:22:04,367
I wonder what they're so happy about.

438
00:22:04,467 --> 00:22:06,000
Tell me about it.

439
00:22:06,100 --> 00:22:07,833
They're literally just washing dishes.

440
00:22:07,933 --> 00:22:08,933
Yeah.

441
00:22:13,900 --> 00:22:14,900
You got it.

442
00:22:14,933 --> 00:22:15,633
- Really?
- Yeah.

443
00:22:15,733 --> 00:22:18,000
These ordinary, unremarkable days...

444
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:19,833
When you eat watermelon,

445
00:22:19,933 --> 00:22:21,667
don't you feel like a rhinoceros beetle?

446
00:22:21,767 --> 00:22:22,967
were just so much fun.

447
00:22:23,067 --> 00:22:24,067
Not really.

448
00:22:24,133 --> 00:22:25,333
What the heck?

449
00:22:25,767 --> 00:22:27,676
This is my first time coming
to a place like this with Rock.

450
00:22:27,700 --> 00:22:28,600
Rock?
I thought days like these...

451
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:32,240
- I'm glad you could come.
- would just naturally continue forever.

452
00:22:32,333 --> 00:22:33,633
That's what I always believed.

453
00:22:34,733 --> 00:22:37,833
It's getting dark earlier now.

454
00:22:38,567 --> 00:22:41,200
Summer is almost over.

455
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:42,067
Yeah.

456
00:22:42,167 --> 00:22:44,500
I don't want it to end.

457
00:22:47,733 --> 00:22:49,033
So-chan, you should come too...

458
00:22:49,133 --> 00:22:50,133
But...

459
00:22:53,600 --> 00:22:54,700
The UK?

460
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:55,800
Yeah.

461
00:22:56,433 --> 00:22:58,300
It's official, I'm going to study abroad.

462
00:23:00,467 --> 00:23:01,267
Huh?

463
00:23:01,366 --> 00:23:03,132
Our time together...

464
00:23:03,233 --> 00:23:04,967
is suddenly coming to an end.

465
00:23:05,067 --> 00:23:06,387
(This drama is purely fictional.)

466
00:23:06,433 --> 00:23:06,967
(Preview for the Final Episode)

467
00:23:07,067 --> 00:23:09,043
(The End of Summer and Time to Say Goodbye)
Let me cancel tomorrow's lesson.

468
00:23:09,067 --> 00:23:10,600
He's avoiding me...

469
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:12,409
(True Feelings That Can't Be Conveyed)
Being honest is the best.

470
00:23:12,433 --> 00:23:14,400
Cry when you want to cry.

471
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:16,276
(A Tearful Farewell Party for Sota)
Of course, everyone has to be there.

472
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:17,867
Natsuki, Sota is leaving.

473
00:23:18,333 --> 00:23:20,200
So-chan, why?

474
00:23:20,300 --> 00:23:21,940
(What Remains After the Storm of Love...)
